window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Rose Cartwright has one primary rule when it comes to college: no dating.</b></p> <p>She's focused on finding the best mocha in Seattle, completing her senior year at Brighton University, working on the school's newspaper, and starting her own company.</p> <p>However, her focus begins to stray when lies start impacting the one person who makes her consider forgetting her rule.</p> <p>Ian Forrest is the starting middle linebacker at Brighton University, known for his grandiose parties and incredible strength and speed on the field. His college career has been focused on one thing: getting drafted into the NFL. His dream has required constant sacrifices, ones he's taken with little regret—until meeting Rose. Has he found the one thing he wants more than a future in football?</p> <p>Two opposing dreams.</p> <p>One conflicting rule.</p> <p>And a website filled with lies that keep threatening to tear them apart.</p> <p><i>This is book five in The Dating Playbook series but can be enjoyed as a complete standalone.</i></p>"; 
